<title>USA: HFS completes Avis buy, plans IPO of unit.</title>
<headline>HFS completes Avis buy, plans IPO of unit.</headline>
<dateline>PARSIPPANY, N.J. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>HFS Inc said that it has completed its acquisition of the world's second largest car rental company, Avis Inc, for approximately $800 million.</p>
<p>HFS also said that it plans to pursue another follow-on acquisition of another car rental company, and in 1997 the company expects to undertake an initial public offering of its majority interest in its rental car subsidiary.</p>
<p>HFS is the largest franchiser of hotels and residential real estate brokerage offices. Its hotel properties include Days Inn, Howard Johnson, Ramada and Super 8. It owns the Century 21, Coldwell Banker and ERA real estate brokers.</p>
</text>
